# The ONE place this repository names the davison/topos kernel revision
# its provenance verifier (cmd/topos-provenance) is built at — read by
# the Makefile (`make verifier`, which the release workflow's signing
# step and `make install-check` both build through). A pinned commit,
# never a floating ref, so the release pipeline can never silently pick
# up a changed manifest format or signing scheme. At a kernel release
# tag since v1.3.0 shipped cmd/topos-provenance (davison/topos#6; the
# tag is commit 7c07400, so the key-set requirement below is checkable
# against it).
#
# The revision must be one whose embedded accepted-key set includes this
# repository's signing key (topos-plugins-2026a, embedded by davison/
# topos@40c1ebd, 16-04): signing never needs the public key, but a
# verifier built before it was embedded rejects every real release —
# which is exactly what the previous pin (e0290110, the commit that
# introduced the CLI) did (davison/topos-plugins#8, the rehearsal).
#
# Known looseness: the kernel's go.mod at this revision does not require
# its own sdk companion module (the kernel workspace resolves it), so
# `go install` resolves github.com/davison/topos/sdk to its latest
# published revision at build time. The verifier's behaviour lives in
# kernel/pluginhost, which IS pinned; the sdk only supplies plugin types.
#
# Comment lines and blank lines are ignored.
v1.3.0
